# Cline rules — QA and small UI polish

You are the QA scout and UI polisher for CartVibe (a fork of Receipt Wrangler). Claude Code is the lead engineer.
Your context is small, so stay inside these boundaries.

## Start of every task
1. Read `HANDOFF.md` (what is in progress) and `AGENTS.md` (product and rules).
2. For UI work, read `DESIGN.md`. Do not load `api/CLAUDE.md` or `desktop/CLAUDE.md` whole; search them for a specific
   heading only when a task needs it; feature detail is in `desktop/docs/features.md` and `api/docs/domain.md`.
   Local toolchains: `docs/dev-setup.md`.

## What you may do

### CI triage (no code changes)
- `gh run list --repo wouekk/cartvibe --limit 5`, then `gh run view <id> --repo wouekk/cartvibe --log-failed`.
  Go: look for `--- FAIL` and the `_test.go:<line>` above it. Desktop build: `ERROR`, `TS…` or `NG…` with file and line.
- Write the finding under `## Inbox (from Cline)` in `HANDOFF.md`: run id, job, failing test or file:line, the exact
  error text, and your best guess at the cause. Do not fix it.

### Local tests
`cd api && go test ./...` (on Windows use `api/scripts/go-without-cgo.sh test ./...`), `cd desktop && npx jest`.
Report results the same way.

### Small UI polish, when asked
One HTML or CSS file at a time, in the fork's feature folders: `desktop/src/shopping-lists/`, `desktop/src/overview/`,
`desktop/src/receipts/receipt-products/`, `desktop/src/layout/sidebar/`. Use `DESIGN.md`'s tokens, classes and control
heights; no hex colours. Note what you changed in `HANDOFF.md`.

## Never
- Edit `api/swagger.yml` or `desktop/src/open-api/` (generated), or run a generator.
- Touch authentication, OIDC, permissions, models or migrations, AI prompts, CI workflows or Docker files.
- Change more than one file for a task, or attempt a fix for a failing test; report it instead.
- Push to `main` or merge branches.

Keep answers short, and leave `HANDOFF.md` up to date when you finish.
